old #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]xprompt_project_identity.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Canonical project-identity resolver[/bold #D7AFFF]                           [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]identity[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]identity: add a single Python helper that normalizes any project [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]spelling (directory key, PROJECT_NAME, alias) to the canonical [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]user-facing namespace name, plus its unit tests.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Namespace and filter the xprompt catalog by user-facing name[/bold #D7AFFF]  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]catalog[dim] · [dim][/dim]after identity[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]catalog: make the xprompt catalog namespace, tag, and filter [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]project-local xprompts by the canonical user-facing project name so [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]requesting project `sase` returns `sase/reads`.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Resolve registry-backed project xprompts independent of cwd[/bold #D7AFFF]   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]resolver[dim] · [dim][/dim]after identity[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]resolver: teach the xprompt loader to read a registered project's [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]checkout xprompts through the project registry so `#sase/reads` expands [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]even when the process cwd is not that checkout.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Normalize the ACE completion project boundary[/bold #D7AFFF]                 [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]tui[dim] · [dim][/dim]after catalog[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]tui: normalize the project identity the ACE prompt bar derives from the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]VCS tag and the prompt context, and add the end-to-end regression test [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]for the reported completion failure.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Mirror the identity fix in the Rust core catalog[/bold #D7AFFF]              [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]core_parity[dim] · [dim][/dim]after catalog[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]core_parity: apply the same canonical-name namespacing and filtering to [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]the Rust xprompt catalog in the sase-core repo so the LSP and gateway [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]agree with Python.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-ac","hidden":false,"llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-5.5","phase_bead_id":"sase-ac.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-139f93092c5339a51cd2efc158405512","started_at":"2026-07-28T07:42:41.113986","state":"dismissed"},{"commits":[{"committed_at":1785243491,"sha":"b449b8a4b5a133ded4771fa07e22307bf97620cb","subject":"fix(xprompt): normalize ACE completion project identity (sase-ac.4)"}],"dismissed_at":"2026-07-28T08:59:16.382515","files":{"chat":{"digest":"78efa1775ecfdb44c9abcdb893a5ccd5a9234588f20bab594113a72fa131169a","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-ac.4/chat.md","size_bytes":5158},"commits":{"digest":"8b9fc8dc25b3b18df5f5c10cd5ab5a97de56cfa15f7b56b80c37fc7c45919a34","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-ac.4/commits.json","size_bytes":245},"meta":{"digest":"afec2b9a70821cc583da9c6e83eed1fac3548a2f6754ea36b3a933b4fea63e5f","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-ac.4/meta.json","size_bytes":554},"state":{"digest":"bb9bfd105de6319b1ec7f9534136e36bc602ae85ab5d0bcb152a1d6fc59391a1","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-ac.4/state.json","size_bytes":225}},"finished_at":"2026-07-28T08:59:16.382515","global_name":"bbugyi200.athena.sase-ac